5. APPLICABLE INDIAN LAWS

   This repository and all its contents are protected under the following 
   Indian statutes. Any violation of this license shall be subject to legal 
   proceedings under one or more of the following laws:

   a) THE COPYRIGHT ACT, 1957 (India)

      - Section 14  — Defines copyright in computer programs and original 
                      literary works. The source code, design, and content 
                      of this repository constitute protected works under 
                      this Act.

      - Section 51  — Any unauthorized reproduction, distribution, or use 
                      of this work constitutes copyright infringement.

      - Section 55  — Entitles the copyright holder (IEEE CIS MJCET) to 
                      civil remedies including injunctions, damages, and 
                      accounts of profits against any infringer.

      - Section 63  — Criminal infringement of copyright is punishable with 
                      imprisonment of not less than 6 months, extendable up 
                      to 3 years, and a fine of not less than ₹50,000, 
                      extendable up to ₹2,00,000.

      - Section 63B — Knowingly making use of an infringing copy of a 
                      computer program is a criminal offence punishable with 
                      imprisonment of not less than 7 days, extendable up to 
                      3 years, and a fine of not less than ₹50,000, 
                      extendable up to ₹2,00,000.

   b) THE INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY ACT, 2000 (India) & AMENDMENT ACT, 2008

      - Section 43  — Any person who without permission of the owner copies, 
                      downloads, extracts, or introduces any computer 
                      contaminant into a computer system shall be liable to 
                      pay damages by way of compensation to the affected party.

      - Section 65  — Tampering with computer source documents (including 
                      source code) is punishable with imprisonment up to 
                      3 years or a fine up to ₹2,00,000, or both.

      - Section 66  — Computer-related offences including unauthorised access, 
                      copying of data, and dishonest use of computer resources 
                      are punishable with imprisonment up to 3 years or a fine 
                      up to ₹5,00,000, or both.

   c) THE BHARATIYA NYAYA SANHITA (BNS), 2023

      - Section 316  — Cheating and dishonestly using or reproducing 
                       property, including intellectual property belonging 
                       to an organization, is a cognizable offence 
                       punishable under this code.

      - Section 303  — Theft of property (including digital property and 
                       intellectual assets) is punishable with imprisonment 
                       and fine as determined by the competent court.

   d) JURISDICTION

      Any disputes arising from the violation of this license shall be 
      subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of courts in Hyderabad, 
      Telangana, India.

6. LEGAL ACTION

   Any unauthorized copying, reproduction, distribution, or use of this 
   codebase — in whole or in part — will be treated as a violation of this 
   license and will result in immediate legal action by the IEEE CIS MJCET 
   organization under the Indian laws cited above, including but not limited 
   to civil injunctions, claims for damages, and criminal prosecution.

